<%# The run drawn as the form that asked for it: the same fields, in the same order, in the
    schedule form's own layout - which is where these fields are already laid out full width
    in a card, the shape this page needs. The Run modal asks the same questions, but its
    label-beside-field grid is sized for a modal and leaves half a page of nothing between
    the two out here.

    A record of a run and the form that starts one are the same set of questions, so they
    are worth reading in the same shape.

    One disabled fieldset carries the read-only-ness, rather than a disabled attribute on
    every control, and there is no form around it: nothing here submits anywhere. Links
    inside a disabled fieldset still work, which is what lets the block rows keep pointing
    at the data they reused.

    Run by and Status are not settings and so have no field in either form. They are drawn
    as plain text under a label of their own rather than squeezed into an input that would
    only lie about being one.

    locals:
      pipeline_job: the run being described %>
<div class='card'>
  <div class='card-body'>
    <fieldset disabled>
      <span class='form-label'>Run by</span>

      <div class='form-control-plaintext pt-0 mb-3'><%= job_launched_by_label(pipeline_job) %></div>

      <span class='form-label'>Status</span>

      <div class='form-control-plaintext pt-0 mb-3'>
        <span class='visually-hidden'>Status: </span>
        <%= job_status_with_icon(nil, pipeline_job) %>
      </div>

      <div class='mb-3'>
        <%= render 'pipeline_jobs/job_blocks', pipeline_job: %>
      </div>

      <%= label_tag 'job-destination', class: 'form-label' do %>
        Destination

        <span
          data-bs-toggle="tooltip"
          data-bs-title="The location this run sent its transformed data to."><i class="bi bi-question-circle" aria-label="helper text"></i>
        </span>
      <% end %>

      <%= select_tag nil, options_for_select([pipeline_job.destination.name]),
                     class: 'form-select mb-3', id: 'job-destination', name: nil %>

      <%= label_tag 'job-delete-previous-records', class: 'form-label' do %>
        Delete Previous Records

        <span
          data-bs-toggle="tooltip"
          data-bs-title="Whether this run deleted every previous record associated with this Source ID."><i class="bi bi-question-circle" aria-label="helper text"></i>
        </span>
      <% end %>

      <%= select_tag nil, options_for_select([job_yes_no(pipeline_job.delete_previous_records)]),
                     class: 'form-select mb-3', id: 'job-delete-previous-records', name: nil %>

      <%= label_tag 'job-run-enrichment-concurrently', class: 'form-label' do %>
        Run Enrichments Concurrently

        <span
          data-bs-toggle="tooltip"
          data-bs-title="Whether this run ran the extractions within an enrichment in parallel. The enrichment's Throttle setting is ignored in that mode."><i class="bi bi-question-circle" aria-label="helper text"></i>
        </span>
      <% end %>

      <%= select_tag nil, options_for_select([job_yes_no(pipeline_job.run_enrichment_concurrently)]),
                     class: 'form-select mb-3', id: 'job-run-enrichment-concurrently', name: nil %>

      <%= label_tag 'job-skip-previously-enriched', class: 'form-label' do %>
        Skip Previously Enriched

        <span
          data-bs-toggle="tooltip"
          data-bs-title="Whether this run applied enrichments only to records that had not previously received them."><i class="bi bi-question-circle" aria-label="helper text"></i>
        </span>
      <% end %>

      <%= select_tag nil, options_for_select([job_yes_no(pipeline_job.skip_previously_enriched)]),
                     class: 'form-select mb-3', id: 'job-skip-previously-enriched', name: nil %>

      <%# Both forms hide this field when the deployment has no priorities configured. A run
          that was given one is still worth reading back, so a job that has one says so
          whether or not the deployment still offers the choice. %>
      <% if ENV['JOB_PRIORITIES'].present? || pipeline_job.job_priority.present? %>
        <%= label_tag 'job-priority', 'Job Priority', class: 'form-label' %>

        <%= select_tag nil, options_for_select([job_priority_label(pipeline_job)]),
                       class: 'form-select mb-3', id: 'job-priority', name: nil %>
      <% end %>
    </fieldset>
  </div>
</div>
